index 0000000..57cecc8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PRIVACY_AUDIT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Privacy audit
+
+Scope: sign-in and sign-up forms, shared page layout, privacy disclosures, and
+document response headers. This was a source review and build check. No browser,
+development server, preview server, or authentication-service requests were used.
+
+## Findings and changes
+
+| Finding | Change |
+| --- | --- |
+| Credentials were sent to an external demo service without an explanation at the form. | Both forms explain the destination and purpose before submission, recommend pseudonyms and unique demo passwords, and link to the privacy policy. Only username and password are submitted. |
+| The shared layout automatically loaded analytics and remote fonts. | Removed the analytics loader, dormant advertising loader, font connections, and remote stylesheet. Brand text uses system serif fonts. Removed the shared advertising slot integration. |
+| Forms displayed raw service error details. | Replaced service errors with fixed messages; no response bodies or tokens are retained by the form. |
+| Request behavior depended on browser defaults. | Explicitly omit cookies and referrers, disable request caching, and reject redirects on authentication requests. |
+| Password state remained after some submission attempts. | Clear password state in the submission cleanup path on success and failure. No credential persistence or logging was added. |
+| Forms had no explicit POST method and lacked password-manager hints. | Added POST methods, named controls, username and password autocomplete, linked helper text, and native sign-up constraints matching the displayed requirements. Controls wait for hydration so a pre-hydration submission cannot bypass the client handler. |
+| Ordinary visits initialized reading-list session state. | Removed eager session initialization; the existing save operation creates state when needed. |
+| Responses lacked explicit privacy boundaries. | Added `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`, a matching document meta fallback, and a `Permissions-Policy` disabling unused camera, microphone, geolocation, and motion sensors. Added `nosniff` and `no-store` for account pages and reading-list responses. |
+| The privacy page used generic boilerplate and the footer linked to a nonexistent preference control. | Replaced the policy with implementation-specific disclosures and linked the footer directly to privacy defaults. |
+
+## Remaining limitations
+
+- The external demo authentication service is outside this repository. Its
+  password handling, logging, retention, access, correction, and deletion processes
+  have not been verified. The forms disclose this and advise against real account
+  information. These controls must be established before using real accounts.
+- The forms display authentication responses but do not establish a persistent
+  authenticated session. They do not store returned tokens.
+- Some article content includes external images and demonstration scripts with
+  their own requests or storage behavior. Removing shared analytics does not
+  audit or remove those demonstrations. The privacy policy makes this distinction.
+- Infrastructure access logs and retention are controlled by the deployment and
+  cannot be established from this repository. Middleware policies apply to
+  application responses; a CDN or reverse proxy must preserve them.
+
+## Validation
+
+- `pnpm run build` succeeds. Astro reports Vite plugin deprecations and ignored
+  `getStaticPaths()` declarations on server-rendered article/category routes.
+- Source review confirms the shared layout has no third-party script or font
+  loaders and both authentication payloads contain only username and password.
+- No end-to-end authentication, browser interaction, or deployed response-header
+  verification was performed.
