+    <p>The forms omit cookies and referrer information from these requests, do not save credentials or returned tokens in browser storage, and clear the password field after each submission attempt. A successful response displays a confirmation; these forms do not establish a persistent signed-in session.</p>
+
+    <h2>Storage and other requests</h2>
+    <p>The site does not initialize a reading-list session just because you visit a page. When you save articles, the reading-list feature uses session storage on the server to remember article identifiers and may use a session cookie to associate the list with your browser.</p>
+    <p>Some articles contain external images or interactive demonstrations that make additional network requests or use browser storage. External image providers can receive your IP address and request headers. The removal of shared analytics does not mean that all article content is free of external resources.</p>
+
+    <h2>Retention and deletion limitations</h2>
+    <p>The external authentication service’s credential storage, retention period, and account access or deletion procedures have not been verified. This demo does not provide account access, correction, or deletion controls. Clearing this site’s browser data does not delete records held by that service. Avoid submitting real personal information.</p>
+    <p>The application source does not establish the hosting provider’s log retention practices. Those practices and the external service’s data controls need to be confirmed before this demonstration is used with real accounts.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
